      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Questions frequently test borrowed sources of the Indian Constitution (e.g., Parliamentary system from UK, Fundamental Rights from US).",
        "Distinction between Federal features (Division of Powers, Bicameralism) and Unitary features (Single Citizenship, Emergency Provisions) is a common exam focus.",
        "Articles related to Fundamental Rights, Directive Principles, and Emergency Provisions are heavily tested in Banking and State/Central competitive exams."
